Cell[TextData[{
 "OK. \n",
 StyleBox["Comment",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ": often (e.g. on Wikipedia, \
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yang%E2%80%93Baxter_equation) you see not \
(12)(23)(13)=(23)(12)(23) like here, but (12)(13)(23)=(23)(13)(12), using all \
three elements, including the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]non-neighbor\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] move (13). As explained in the FYAD11 course notes \
and homework problems (at the time of writing, 1.9.7), to generate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["S", "3"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8238431b-16e2-4dc4-8855-61838fec0d27"],
 " it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s enough to use ",
 StyleBox["local moves",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (exchange of neighbors). Using only nearest-neighbor exchanges is the \
Coxeter presentation of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["S", "n"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "54e4e9b3-e264-48a2-8219-87fce2a063a5"],
 ":\[LineSeparator]https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coxeter_group\[LineSeparator]\
For example in Zee\[CloseCurlyQuote]s book on group theory, he says \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 StyleBox["exchanges are the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]atoms\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] out of which permutations are built",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], but he doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t then restrict to \
local moves (I think). \n\nOn a discrete lattice, allowing only local moves \
is sufficient to permute three classical objects, but amounts to what ",
 StyleBox["range",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " we want to allow our interactions to have: nearest-neighbor, \
next-to-nearest neighbor, and so on. For more on this, see below.\n\nAssemble \
a quantum circuit of Braid acting on successive states.\nHere\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s (23)(12)(23):"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.976894355193349*^9, 3.9768943851624002`*^9}, {
  3.9768945564634037`*^9, 3.976894562552719*^9}, {3.9769559150161867`*^9, 
  3.976955941383119*^9}, {3.9769560716619873`*^9, 3.976956071992053*^9}, {
  3.976956106234926*^9, 3.976956137099987*^9}, {3.976956195751651*^9, 
  3.976956211664628*^9}, {3.976956278923073*^9, 3.9769562799972363`*^9}, {
